# Session and claims

Authentication should be **cheap and local** on every request (`getClaims` / JWT verify). Occasional JWKS fetch or token refresh is normal.

**Do not keep optimizing `getClaims()` / middleware** unless a new scan shows they are slow again. Page data is the remaining target after a warm JWKS.

## Keep

- JWT role in middleware (`role=0ms` when claims carry role).
- `Promise.all(profile, permissions)` on session_pack MISS when `claimsRole` is set — time each promise independently.
- Process-TTL session shell HIT (must stay cheap: claims + map lookup).
- Process-global JWKS (`lib/auth/jwks-cache.ts` on `globalThis`) passed into `getClaims({ jwks })`. Warm at login. Middleware and RSC must share this cache — do not let each bundle HTTP-fetch `jwks.json` on the first authenticated hop.

## Session pack logs

- `HIT` — shell cache hit only. If this is hundreds of ms, look at `client=` (Supabase client/cookies), not the cache.
- `WAIT` — another request is already building the shell (singleflight). Not a cache hit.
- `MISS` — this request built profile + permissions.

Warm the shell at **login** (`setCachedSessionShell`) so the first panel hop is a HIT.

## getClaims

Do not replace `getClaims` with `getUser`. Do not skip per-request claims.
Use `getClaimsWithSharedJwks` (not a bare `client.auth.getClaims()`) on middleware and RSC.

## Panel links

One navigator per target. Table/detail `<Link>`s use `prefetch={false}` unless prefetch is intentional.
